  "notes": "Listed on HCA page as 'July 1, 2026 to present - Dental program fee schedule (published June 23, 2026)'. child = column 'Max fee Dental ages 0-20'; adult = 'Max fee Dental ages 21+'. For D8xxx orthodontic codes the child value comes from column 'Max fee Ortho ages 0-20' (no adult ortho fee). Separate higher ABCD (Access to Baby and Child Dentistry) column not recorded (e.g. D0120 ABCD 41.24, D0150 56.53, D2140 89.05). D1351 adult fee $32.97 is marked '**' = services only for eligible DDA clients 21 and over; D4355 is 'DDA coverage only'. Many codes require PA/EPA (e.g. D2740-D2752 crowns child-only with PA for ages 15-20; no adult crown fee listed). Codes absent from the schedule: implants, bridges (D62xx/D67xx), partials D5213/D5214/D5225/D5226, interim D5820/D5821. Most Apple Health clients are in managed care for medical but dental is FFS via ProviderOne (Apple Health dental is fee-for-service statewide).",
